  "description": "T-4253: the labels Excel writes when it relabels a decimal numeric pivot group. Each pivot groups its row field by numeric ranges with a <groupItems> list one item too long, every item a wrong text (w0, w1, ...), so Excel replaces it with its own labels: P by 0.1 from 0 to 1, Q by 0.1 from 1.1 to 2.1, R by 0.001 from 0 to 0.01, S by 0.25 from -1 to 1, T by 1e-5 from 0 to 1e-4, U by 0.3 from 0 to 1.5, V by 1/3 from 0 to 1, W by 12345678901.2 from 0 to 123456789012. Each field has one record below the start, one inside each group and one past the end. Calc reads the cells Excel renders (rows 3 on, as text), two columns per pivot.",
